<article class="env-lemma" id="067L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/067L">Lemma <span data-tag="067L">29.33.18</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z \ar[r]_ i \ar[rd]_ j &  X \ar[d] \\  &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of schemes where $i$ and $j$ are immersions. Then there is a canonical exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{C}_{Z/Y} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \to i^*\Omega _{X/Y} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> where the first arrow comes from Lemma <a href="/tag/01R4" data-tag="01R4">29.32.3</a> and the second from Lemma <a href="/tag/01UZ" data-tag="01UZ">29.33.15</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The algebraic version of this is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/065V" data-tag="065V">10.134.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>